  {
   "seq": 3,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "Use a ConfigMap for setting configuration data separately from application code.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "使用 ConfigMap 将配置 data 与应用代码分开设置。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": null,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "ConfigMap",
     "target": "ConfigMap",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "data",
     "target": "data",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false,
   "tmHits": []
  },
  {
   "seq": 4,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "For example, imagine that you are developing an application that you can run on your\nown computer (for development) and in the cloud (to handle real traffic).\nYou write the code to look in an environment variable named `DATABASE_HOST`.\nLocally, you set that variable to `localhost`. In the cloud, you set it to\nrefer to a Kubernetes Service\nthat exposes the database component to your cluster.\nThis lets you fetch a container image running in the cloud and\ndebug the exact same code locally if needed.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "例如，设想你正在开发一个应用，该应用既可以在你自己的\n计算机上运行（用于开发），也可以在云中运行（用于处理真实流量）。\n你编写代码来查找名为 `DATABASE_HOST` 的环境变量。\n在本地，你将该变量设置为 `localhost`。在云中，你将其设置为\n引用一个 Kubernetes Service，\n该 Service 向你的集群公开数据库组件。\n这样，如果需要，你可以获取一个在云中运行的容器映像，并在本地\n调试完全相同的代码。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": null,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
    {
     "source": "container",
     "target": "容器",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Kubernetes",
     "target": "Kubernetes",
     "compliant": true
    },
    {
     "source": "Service",
     "target": "Service",
     "compliant": true
    }
   ],
   "edited": false,
   "tmHits": []
  },
  {
   "seq": 5,
   "blockType": "paragraph",
   "level": null,
   "prefix": "",
   "source": "A ConfigMap is not designed to hold large chunks of data. The data stored in a\nConfigMap cannot exceed 1 MiB. If you need to store settings that are\nlarger than this limit, you may want to consider mounting a volume or use a\nseparate database or file service.",
   "suffix": "\n\n",
   "translatable": true,
   "chunkIndex": 1,
   "target": "ConfigMap 并非用于存储大块 data。存储在 ConfigMap 中的 data\n不能超过 1 MiB。如果需要存储大于此限制的设置，可以考虑挂载卷，或使用\n单独的数据库或文件 Service。",
   "status": "DONE",
   "reviewScore": null,
   "reviewRounds": 0,
   "compliance": [
